# Show how each comment was handled; resolve or reopen it

## What to build

KAN-19 (spec `docs/prd/06-human-review-round.md` §7.5, story 3 and 4). When the run pauses again after a human round, every comment from earlier rounds shows its **outcome** next to it, and the user decides what happens to it:

- **Outcome** for each comment, taken from the last review round:
  - the fixer note (`reports/round<N>/fixer-comments.json`), or "no note";
  - the code reviewer verdict and evidence (`code.json` → `comments`);
  - for `liveCheck` comments, the live tester's verdict for the case with the same id (`tester.json` → `cases`).
- **Resolve**: sets `status: "resolved"`. The comment no longer goes to the fixer, reviewer or tester.
- **Reopen**: sets `status: "reopened"`, with an optional follow-up text appended to `followUps`. It goes out again on the next Request changes.

Only the human changes a comment's status. The reviewer's verdict never resolves or reopens a comment by itself. `POST /review/changes` is allowed when at least one comment is `open` or `reopened`, as it is already. The web view gets a "Previous comments" section with these outcomes and buttons.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- Already built:
  - `src/review/human.ts`:
    - `Comment` (`id` like `H1-2`, `round`, `file?`, `line?`, `snippet?`, `body`, `liveCheck`, `status: open|resolved|reopened`, `followUps: string[]`);
    - `humanRoundPath`, `loadHumanRound`, `saveHumanRound` (atomic);
    - `allComments(runDir, upToRound)`;
    - `HumanReviewStore` (`current`, `add`, `edit`, `remove`; edits are allowed only on the current round and serialized);
    - `openComments`;
    - `readFixerNotes(runDir, round)` → `Record<id, note>`;
    - `fixerCommentsPath`.
  - `src/review/report.ts`:
    - `Report.comments?: { id; verdict: "addressed" | "not_addressed"; evidence? }[]`;
    - `Report.cases?` (tester verdicts `pass|fail|blocked` with `evidence`).
  - `src/review/phase.ts`:
    - `readReport(file, round, kind)` (165-175);
    - `reviewReportPath(runDir, round, kind)`;
    - `loadRound(runDir, round)` (211-220).
    - Review state `round` is the last review round, and `humanRound` is the current pause.
  - `src/web/server.ts`:
    - `GET /review` → `{ round, blocking, files, comments, diffBase, diffHead }`;
    - `POST/PUT/DELETE /review/comments[/<id>]`;
    - `POST /review/changes`;
    - `readJson`, the 409 helper, the `/review/` prefix parsing, and the `human: { runDir, repo }` option.
  - `src/web/page.html`: review banner, diff with inline comment forms, current-round comment list with Edit/Delete, and **Request changes**.
- `src/web/page.html` patterns:
  - `renderPlan(box, tp)` (441-459) shows verdict badges `v-<verdict>` and evidence that expands on click;
  - `failureSection` (284-315) shows the button pattern.
- Tests:
  - `src/review/human.test.ts`;
  - `src/web/server.test.ts`: `setup()` (15-26), `post(...)`, and the route describe blocks.

## Patterns to follow

**Status changes** (`HumanReviewStore`, in the file of the comment's own round):
```ts
resolve(id: string): Promise<Comment>;                    // only comments of earlier rounds (c.round < current round)
reopen(id: string, followUp?: string): Promise<Comment>;  // trims followUp; empty → no follow-up
```
- An unknown id throws `HumanReviewError` (404).
- A current-round comment throws (400: "edit or delete it instead").

**Outcome** (`human.ts`):
```ts
export interface CommentOutcome {
  fixerNote?: string;
  verdict?: "addressed" | "not_addressed";
  evidence?: string;
  liveCheck?: { verdict: "pass" | "fail" | "blocked"; evidence?: string };
}
/** Outcome of each comment in the last review round (`reports/round<round>/`); {} for comments not sent there. */
export async function commentOutcomes(runDir: string, round: number, comments: readonly Comment[]): Promise<Record<string, CommentOutcome>>
```
- Read `code.json` and `tester.json` of that round with `readReport` from `src/review/phase.ts`. If importing from `phase.ts` would create an import cycle, move `readReport`/`reviewReportPath` to `src/review/report.ts`.
- Read the fixer notes with `readFixerNotes`. Fix passes write notes in the same round folder as the review that follows them (`round<N>`), so use the same `round`.

## Step-by-step tasks

### UPDATE `src/review/human.ts` (+ tests)
- **IMPLEMENT**: `resolve`, `reopen` and `commentOutcomes`.
- **VALIDATE**: `npx vitest run src/review/human.test.ts`. Cover:
  - resolve and reopen persist to the right round file;
  - a follow-up is appended;
  - a resolved comment is excluded from `openComments` and a reopened one is included;
  - outcomes merge note, verdict and live-check verdict;
  - missing report files → empty outcome.

### UPDATE `src/web/server.ts` (+ tests)
- **IMPLEMENT**:
  - `GET /review` adds `outcomes: Record<id, CommentOutcome>` for the last review round (review state `round`). The server can read it from `store.getState()`; if it isn't there, include `round` in the `review:waiting` event payload and store it in `ViewState.review.reviewRound`.
  - `POST /review/comments/<id>/resolve` → 200 with the comment.
  - `POST /review/comments/<id>/reopen` with body `{ followUp?: string }` → 200 with the comment.
  - Both routes return 409 when the run is not waiting.
- **VALIDATE**: `npx vitest run src/web/server.test.ts`

### UPDATE `src/web/page.html`
- **IMPLEMENT**: a "Previous comments" section in the review screen, one card per earlier-round comment:
  - id, location (`file:line` or "general"), the snippet in a `pre`, the body and follow-ups;
  - **Fixer:** the note or "no note";
  - **Reviewer:** an `addressed` / `not addressed` badge plus evidence that expands;
  - **Live check:** a `pass` / `fail` / `blocked` badge, reusing the `v-<verdict>` styles from `renderPlan`;
  - the status, and **Resolve** / **Reopen** buttons. Reopen opens a small textarea for the follow-up and a confirm button.
  - Cards are pinned to their own round (no remapping onto the new diff).
  - A header counter: `N comments · A addressed · R resolved`.
- **GOTCHA**: the page re-fetches `GET /review` after every action; keep the `row.seq` stale-response guard pattern.

### ADD an end-to-end test (`src/review/phase.test.ts` or `src/runner/run.test.ts`)
- **IMPLEMENT**: two human rounds:
  - round 1: comment H1-1 → changes; the reviewer reports `addressed`;
  - round 2: `GET /review` (or `commentOutcomes`) shows the note and the verdict; reopen H1-1 with a follow-up → changes → the fixer prompt contains the follow-up;
  - round 3: resolve H1-1 → `POST /review/changes` → 409 (nothing open) → apply → exit 0.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] At each pause after a human round, each earlier comment shows the fixer note, the reviewer verdict with evidence, and the live-check result (if any)
- [ ] Resolve and reopen (with follow-up) persist and survive `--resume`
- [ ] Resolved comments are never sent again; reopened ones are, including their follow-ups
- [ ] Only the human changes a comment's status
- [ ] Routes return 409 when not waiting, 404 for an unknown id, and 400 for a current-round comment
- [ ] `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` pass

## Validation commands

```bash
npm run typecheck && npm run lint
npx vitest run src/review src/web
npm run build && npx vitest run src/web-e2e.test.ts
```
